# AIDEN Research OS — CODEOWNERS
#
# Primary owner is required for ALL paths.
# Security-critical paths require BOTH primary and a secondary reviewer.
#
# Rationale: audit finding HIGH-01 — single CODEOWNER is a single point of failure.
# Resolution: Security-critical boundaries require 2-person review.
# ADR reference: ADR-0009 (Research Lab Security Test Plan)
#
# Secondary reviewer (@security-reviewer) should be a trusted human who is NOT
# the primary operator of AIDEN. Can be a colleague, collaborator, or second
# GitHub account you control that you treat as a separate review identity.
# Update @security-reviewer to the actual account before merging this file.

# ── Default: primary owner required for all files ──────────────────────────
*                                   @repo-owner

# ── Governance artifacts: primary required ──────────────────────────────────
/docs/                              @repo-owner
/research/                          @repo-owner
/codex/                             @repo-owner
/schemas/                           @repo-owner
/fixtures/                          @repo-owner

# ── SECURITY-CRITICAL: requires primary + secondary approval ────────────────
# These paths define the hard boundaries and approval semantics. A compromise
# here undermines the entire governance model.

SAFETY.md                           @repo-owner @security-reviewer
AGENTS.md                           @repo-owner @security-reviewer
/docs/system/PRODUCT_BOUNDARY.md    @repo-owner @security-reviewer
/docs/system/EXECUTION_BOUNDARY.md  @repo-owner @security-reviewer
/docs/security/                     @repo-owner @security-reviewer
/research/ledgers/approval-record.md @repo-owner @security-reviewer
/research/ledgers/phase-gate-record.md @repo-owner @security-reviewer
/.github/workflows/                 @repo-owner @security-reviewer
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @repo-owner @security-reviewer
/scripts/validate-governance.sh     @repo-owner @security-reviewer
/schemas/governance/phase-gate-record.schema.json @repo-owner @security-reviewer
/schemas/secret-manager/            @repo-owner @security-reviewer
